{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563178,"nonce":"cWr0zQxlCPWc5oad3hD83e5+STk=","title":"Events, focus and keyboard: dispatch on the scene","message":"blinc_ts hands an app raw xwindow events and a hit-test; every app does its own dispatch. A framework needs the platform's event model, as ashui provides in haxe/ashui/input (Events, Pointer, Keyboard, Focus, Scroll, Clipboard, Interaction; about 1,500 lines).\n\n**Scope**\n- Pointer events dispatched to the hit node with capture and bubbling, stopPropagation and preventDefault; enter, leave, over, out; pointer capture during a drag; click and double-click; the cursor from the node under the pointer.\n- Interaction state for CSS: :hover, :active, :focus, :focus-visible, :disabled, kept by the SDK and fed to the cascade.\n- Focus: focusable nodes, tab order, focus and blur events, focus-visible after keyboard use, focus scopes for dialogs.\n- Keyboard: keydown and keyup with key and code, modifiers, repeat; text input separately from keys; IME composition events.\n- Wheel and scrolling: scroll containers from overflow, wheel and trackpad deltas with momentum, nested containers passing the wheel on at their edge, scrollbars.\n- Clipboard read and write.","files":null}]}